Description: An individual-level, stochastic, open-cohort microsimulation for
    modelling population demographics, body mass index (BMI) trajectories,
    mortality, and obesity-related health and economic outcomes among adults in
    Portugal over the period 1998–2040. The model comprises three modules:
    (1) BMI trajectory simulation using empirical transition matrices derived
    from the Portuguese National Health Survey; (2) health burden estimation
    (years of life lost, quality-adjusted life years, and disability-adjusted
    life years); and (3) obesity-attributable healthcare cost projection.
    The package is designed to support population-level policy analysis,
    including budget-allocation and targeting scenarios for obesity interventions.
